direction: down

title: |md
  ## NAPI: cooperative polled RX
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

before: "Pure-IRQ era (pre-NAPI)" {
  style.fill: "#fee2e2"
  b_body: |md
    - Every packet → one IRQ
    - Driver runs RX in IRQ context

    **Problem at high rates:**
    - 1 Mpps = 1M IRQs/s
    - Receive livelock
    - CPU spends all time in IRQ
    - Other work starves
  |
}

napi: "NAPI hybrid (modern)" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  n_body: |md
    - First packet → IRQ
    - napi_schedule() raises softirq
    - Driver disables further IRQs
    - Polls until budget exhausted

    **Wins:**
    - One IRQ per burst, not per packet
    - Bounded work:
    - `napi->poll(napi, budget)`
    - Caller (softirq) yields at budget
    - Re-enables IRQs when no more work
  |
}

budget: |md
  **Budget mechanism:**
  - Default `net.core.netdev_budget = 300`
  - 300 packets per softirq run
  - `netdev_budget_usecs = 2000`
  - Max 2ms per softirq run
  - Hit either limit → return early
  - Reschedules, continues next softirq tick
| {style.fill: "#fef3c7"}

before -> napi: "evolved" {style.stroke-dash: 4}
napi -> budget
